README policy entry: - `POST /v1/policies` creates a versioned release policy scoped to a tenant and workload. The JSON body must include non-empty `tenant_id`, `workload_id`, `name` and `rule`. A rule is exactly one of a leaf carrying one locator (`{"claim": "<top-level claim name>"}` or `{"path": ["<segment>", ...]}`) and exactly one comparison, or a compound node `{"all": [rule, ...]}`, `{"any": [rule, ...]}` (both non-empty lists) or `{"not": rule}`; any other shape is rejected with `422`. The comparisons are `equals` with one scalar (scalar = string, finite number, boolean or null), `in` with one to 32 unique scalars, `containsAll` with one to 32 unique scalars, `lt`/`lte`/`gt`/`gte` against one finite JSON number, and `exists: true`; for example `{"claim": "labels", "containsAll": ["measured", "boot"]}` or `{"path": ["meta", "labels"], "containsAll": ["eu"]}`. A `containsAll` candidate list must be a n
